      "writtenOn": "2022-03-23T05:04:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "i wonder if rpm_diff should be based on RPM_MARGIN.\n\nsome recent devices like vell set RPM_DEVIATION to 1% while\nthe default is 7%. if such a fan is used on another device,\nwe\u0027ll get a different ramp up and i don\u0027t think it should\nbe different. this strange fan behavior will result in\nfan_duty_adjust(..., 1%, ...) in on vell but\nfan_duty_adjust(..., 7%, ...) in the default case.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 304,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 304,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "c59d59273ae08b99a6280a5a7ea617bcb3d4b376",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8a8753a0_36c6213c",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/fan.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 304,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132339
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-23T08:39:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The driver can adjust the PWM duty only if rpm_diff is greater than the deviation [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/chip/npcx/fan.c;l\u003d306). \nSet \"rpm_diff \u003d RPM_MARGIN(rpm_target) + 1\" to make sure fan_adjust_duty() can be called while also increase the PWM duty with low steps.\nIt can help bypass the 100% spin issue at the beginning.\nOnce the 1 second passes, the driver go back to use the original fan control algorithm.",
      "parentUuid": "488f7ea6_5149919c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 304,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 304,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "c59d59273ae08b99a6280a5a7ea617bcb3d4b376",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "032c8c54_be8e4e26",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/fan.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 304,
      "author": {
        "id": 1190764
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-23T09:06:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "right, i\u0027m wondering about the case where the board leaves\nRPM_MARGIN at 7%. will it still ramp as smoothly as 1%?",
      "parentUuid": "8a8753a0_36c6213c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 304,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 304,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "c59d59273ae08b99a6280a5a7ea617bcb3d4b376",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4decfc8c_4247de88",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/fan.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 304,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132339
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-23T09:49:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When the rpm_target \u003c\u003d 3557,\nfor 1% : rpm_diff \u003d 3557 * 1%  +1 \u003d 36\nfor 7% \" rpm_diff \u003d 3557 * 7%  +1 \u003d 249\nAccording to [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/chip/npcx/fan.c;l\u003d264), the increasing duty step is the same.\nWhen the rpm_target \u003e 3557\nfor 1% : rpm_diff \u003d 3558 * 1%  +1 \u003d 36\nfor 7% \" rpm_diff \u003d 3557 * 7%  +1 \u003d 250\nThe increasing duty step is 1 for 1% and 3 for 7%.\nSearch the whole EC source, the existing rpm_max value \u003d 6900. That’s being said, the duty step should be either 1 or 3 depending on the target RPM and deviation. \nI played the fan control on Volteer which uses 7% deviation, I don\u0027t see the fan spin unsmooth with target RPM 2200~5400.\nIf you still have concern on the setting, how about change the code to use fixed rpm_diff like\n```\nrpm_diff \u003d MAX(250, RPM_MARGIN(rpm_target) + 1);\n```",
      "parentUuid": "032c8c54_be8e4e26",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 304,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 304,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "c59d59273ae08b99a6280a5a7ea617bcb3d4b376",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
